# Overview

Scholarly publishing has always balanced fidelity against flexibility. The data
science literature provides a useful frame for this tension [@jones2019], while
applied work in climate science shows why reproducible artifacts matter
[@smith2020].

# Analysis

Accessible explanations of new methods accelerate adoption [@lee2021]. Chicago
author-date citation, used throughout this report, keeps sources legible within
the running prose [@smith2020, p. 50].

# Conclusion

A deterministic toolchain lets historians and scientists alike cite with
confidence.

